MENTOR: I eased Title › Position between 0.5 s and 1.5 s. If you want it back the way it was, use **Edit > Undo**.

That frame at 1 s is the middle of the move. Before, Title crossed from 0.5 s to 1.5 s at a constant speed, then stopped dead. That's what linear means: no build-up and no slowing down, so it looks mechanical. Easing makes the motion slow into and out of each keyframe.

Two things to look at now:
- The two keyframes on Position changed shape. They were diamonds and now look rounded.
- Scrub through 0.5 s to 1.5 s. The motion should now start gently and settle gently.

To do this yourself, select the keyframes, then choose **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease** (or press F9). In the Graph Editor, a straight line means linear and an S-curve means eased.

The demo is the only one I'll do, so the rest of Title is yours:
- **Position,** 1.5 s to 3 s
- **Scale,** 0.5 s to 1.5 s
- **Opacity,** 0.5 s to 1.5 s

Tell me when you're done and I'll check.

